  "reference_protocol": "Both public Core file modes compare return code, complete output, first diagnostic, persisted catalog/table rowids/rows and SQLite integrity. Named physical-record and view metadata controls additionally check view rootpage, catalog rowids, schema versions and actual VIEW reads. Final seed is fresh. No expected-answer routing, masking, filters or output correction is used.",
  "implementation": [
    "Persistent view sources carry a CoreTokenGrammar certificate tying the actual SQL text to its exact CREATE VIEW definition. Name/width errors are deferred until preparation, as in SQLite. Views are separate source-aware Core.State metadata; the original Core.Database table model and equivalence are unchanged.",
    "CoreViewSQL loads actual sqlite_schema rowids and the header schema cookie. Source/compiler metadata maintains independent durable/transaction/savepoint snapshots. Intrinsic rowid sorting only permutes existing checked table objects.",
    "Private view materialization clears caller CTE and scalar scopes and preserves the declared visible columns, first-projection collations and original type names. Scalar SELECT column origins supply type metadata without evaluating row values. PRAGMA table functions evaluate their arguments once and share actual view source inspection.",
    "The independent concrete grammar can replay one referenced WITH source retained in the current view AST. Optional reference tracing records AST roles and actual token positions. ALTER resolves column/table references in their lexical source scopes, edits only the corresponding spans, retains untouched SQL trivia and independently certifies the resulting source. Pre/post ALTER preparation rejects invalid dependent views before publication.",
    "Catalog encoding retains actual schema identities and root-zero VIEW records. Rollback writes independently decode/check the actual object catalog and header cookie before journal activation; WAL independently decodes/checks its actual encoded object records before append. Existing table/index component checks remain.",
    "Foreign page-size rollback writes use an explicitly separate atomic whole-image conversion with the same independent catalog/object checks. WAL keeps its existing geometry. Successful publication acknowledges actual durable object metadata, including view-only commits and rollbacks."
  ],
  "proof_scope": "Registered component theorems certify actual VIEW source decoding, deterministic definitions for equal SQL, metadata acknowledgement, unchanged table state under object transitions, permutation of complete Core tables under catalog ordering, unrelated rename identity, actual image/object attachment and preservation of the ordinary table-only publication guard. Existing table/index/rollback component contracts are retained. No full SQL equivalence, full ALTER resolver correctness theorem, unbounded concurrency result or universal SQLite compatibility is claimed.",
  "feature_probe_scope": "The 88-case unittest and fresh survey share named families and a generator. Twelve remaining failures are six families in two file modes: triggers, WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys, partial indexes, expression indexes and UTF-16 reading. These are not a global compatibility percentage.",
