  "limitations": [
    "Temporary views and the full WITH view surface (including unused/multiple/recursive CTE forms not retained in the current view AST) remain separate work.",
    "General planner flattening/expression-demand elimination, wider scalar/derived origin metadata, schema namespaces, view column-name collision rules, complex ALTER/USING/window bindings and wider invalid-view error priorities are not exhausted by this suite.",
    "Rollback conversion changes the physical page size to 4096 and uses atomic replacement, not the same-geometry rollback-journal trace. This checkpoint does not claim identical page geometry or coverage of every conversion crash/concurrent schedule.",
    "Trigger execution, WITHOUT ROWID, composite keys, expression/partial indexes, UTF-16, VIRTUAL generated columns, non-BINARY indexes and the previously documented wider SQL/storage gaps remain. Existing unsupported trigger metadata blocks writes rather than being silently discarded.",
    "Nonpositive or out-of-range schema catalog rowids and unsupported retained view SQL fail closed. The finite target/probe and SIGKILL sets do not exhaust SQLite SQL, DB/WAL format, failure, concurrency or host-service behavior."
